draw(dir(120)--dir(120)*4/7);
draw(dir(180)--dir(180)*4/7);
draw(dir(240)--dir(240)*4/7);
draw(dir(300)--dir(300)*4/7);

draw(unitcircle);
[/asy]

This is a pretty funny problem: personally, I spent a lot of time wondering why these specific numbers were chosen until I had the "Aha!" moment.

<details><summary>Solution</summary>The main observation is that
\[2^{-1} + 2^{-2} + 2^{-3} + 2^{-4} + 2^{-5} + 2^{-6} + 2^{-10} = \frac{2018}{2048}.\]
With this observation, the problem is straightforward. Let  $T = \{1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 10\}$  for convenience and note that
\begin{align*}
\left(\frac{2018}{2048}\right)^{2018}
& = (2^{-1} + 2^{-2} + 2^{-3} + 2^{-4} + 2^{-5} + 2^{-6} + 2^{-10})^{2018}
& = \sum_{a_1, \dots, a_{2018} \in T} 2^{-(a_1 + \dots + a_{2018})}
& \ge \sum_{\substack{a_1, \dots, a_{2018} \in T  a_1 + \dots + a_{2018} = 3860}} 2^{-(a_1 + \dots + a_{2018})}
& = 2^{-3860} |S|
\end{align*}
which solves the problem.</details>

