The main claim is that  $P$  and  $Q$  are precisely the intersection points of the circles  $\omega$  and  $\Gamma$ . To show this, we invert at  $R$ . Let  $X^*$  denote the inverse of point  $X$ . Since  $AB<AC$ , this means that  $A^*B^*>A^*C^*$ .

