let  $\angle DPA=\alpha$  and  $\angle PQD=\beta$  now  $\angle PDQ +\angle PCQ= 90+90=180$  so we have  $PDQC$  is cyclic.   $\angle QPD = 90-\beta$  so  $\angle APF= 90 +\beta-\alpha$  now  $\angle DPC =180- \alpha$  and as  $PDQC$  is cyclic we have  $\angle DQC=\alpha$ and so we have  $\angle CQP =\angle DQC -\angle DQP= \alpha -\beta$  . Cyclicity of  $PDQC$  also gives  $\angle BDC \equiv\angle PDC =\angle PQC =\alpha-\beta$  and now as  $ABCD$  is cyclic we conclude  $\angle BDC=\angle CAB=\alpha-\beta$  and so we get  $\angle PFA= 180-(\angle PAF + \angle APF)=180-(\alpha-\beta+90 +\beta-\alpha)=180-90=90$  and so we are done  $\blacksquare$ .
