and taking  $t = cos(x)$  we obtain: $y(t) = 128t^8-256t^6+184t^4-50t^2+2t+1$  (i).

The first derivative of (i) yields the real critical values: $y'(t) = 1024t^7-1536t^5+736t^3-100t+2 = 0 \Rightarrow t = -0.5, 0.0200594, 0.454901$  (ii);

and a second derivative check of (ii) produces: $y''(t) = 7168t^6 -7680t^4+2208t^2-100 \Rightarrow y''(-0.5) = 84, y''(0.0200594)=-99.113, y''(0.454901)=91.5572$  (iii).

Taking the positive values of (iii) ultimately gives us  $y(-0.5) =-4.5, y(0.454901)=-2.5915 \Rightarrow y_{MIN} = $  $\fbox{-4.5}$ .

